<title>USA: Conrail fire disrupts N.J. train service.</title>
<headline>Conrail fire disrupts N.J. train service.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>All Northeast Corridor train service has been stopped by a fire in a Conrail Inc freight train on the south side of New Brunswick, N.J., Amtrak spokesman Rick Remington.</p>
<p>He said NJ TRANSIT, which operates trains carrying commuters from New York City and Newark, N.J., is holding trains serving the Metro Park, Metuchen, Edison, New Brunswick, Princeton and Trenton stations at Newark.</p>
<p>Conrail spokesmen were not immediately available to comment on the status of the fire.</p>
<p>((-- Jim Brumm 212-859-1710.))</p>
</text>
